concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 1."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-1 ;
    values:originalText "For the purpose of this Convention the term “discrimination” includes— (a) any distinction, exclusion or preference made on the basis of race, colour, sex, religion, political opinion, national extraction or social origin, which has the effect of nullifying or impairing equality of opportunity or treatment in employment or occupation;  Schedule 1  Convention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and Occupation  Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) such other distinction, exclusion or preference which has the effect of nullifying or impairing equality of opportunity or treatment in employment or occupation as may be determined by the Member concerned after consultation with representative employer’s and worker’s organisations, where such exist, and with other appropriate bodies. 2. Any distinction, exclusion or preference in respect of a particular job based on the inherent requirements thereof shall not be deemed to be discrimination. 3. For the purpose of this Convention the terms “employment” and “occupation” include access to vocational training, access to employment and to particular occupations, and terms and conditions of employment." ;
    skos:definition "For the purpose of this Convention the term “discrimination” includes— (a) any distinction, exclusion or preference made on the basis of race, colour, sex, religion, political opinion, national extraction or social origin, which has the effect of nullifying or impairing equality of opportunity or treatment in employment or occupation;  Schedule 1  Convention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and Occupation  Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) such other distinction, exclusion or preference which has the effect of nullifying or impairing equality of opportunity or treatment in employment or occupation as may be determined by the Member concerned after consultation with representative employer’s and worker’s organisations, where such exist, and with other appropriate bodies. 2. Any distinction, exclusion or preference in respect of a particular job based on the inherent requirements thereof shall not be deemed to be discrimination. 3. For the purpose of this Convention the terms “employment” and “occupation” include access to vocational training, access to employment and to particular occupations, and terms and conditions of employment."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "af675236a5049ee18b8f462238d4e23da6becf0fcd229b2cf410a152ea238437" ;
    cof:pageNumber "125"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Discrimination includes distinctions, exclusions or preferences affecting equality of opportunity or treatment in employment or occupation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.125" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-norm .
