concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 1."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-8 ;
    values:originalText "This Convention shall be binding only upon those Members of the International Labour Organisation whose ratifications have been registered with the Director-General. 2. It shall come into force twelve months after the date on which the ratifications of two Members have been registered with the Director-General.  Schedule 1  Convention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and Occupation  Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  3. Thereafter, this Convention shall come into force for any Member twelve months after the date on which its ratification has been registered." ;
    skos:definition "This Convention shall be binding only upon those Members of the International Labour Organisation whose ratifications have been registered with the Director-General. 2. It shall come into force twelve months after the date on which the ratifications of two Members have been registered with the Director-General.  Schedule 1  Convention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and Occupation  Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  3. Thereafter, this Convention shall come into force for any Member twelve months after the date on which its ratification has been registered."@en ;
