concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-8-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 1."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-8-2 ;
    values:originalText "No one shall be held in slavery; slavery and the slave-trade in all their forms shall be prohibited. 2. No one shall be held in servitude.  Schedule 2  International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  3. (a) No one shall be required to perform forced or compulsory labour; (b) Paragraph 3(a) shall not be held to preclude, in countries where imprisonment with hard labour may be imposed as a punishment for a crime, the performance of hard labour in pursuance of a sentence to such punishment by a competent court; (c) For the purpose of this paragraph the term “forced or compulsory labour” shall not include:  (i) Any work or service, not referred to in sub-paragraph (b), normally required of a person who is under detention in consequence of a lawful order of a court, or of a person during conditional release from such detention;  (ii) Any service of a military character and, in countries where conscientious objection is recognized, any national service required by law of conscientious objectors;  (iii) Any service exacted in cases of emergency or calamity threatening the life or well-being of the community;  (iv) Any work or service which forms part of normal civil obligations." ;
    skos:definition "No one shall be held in slavery; slavery and the slave-trade in all their forms shall be prohibited. 2. No one shall be held in servitude.  Schedule 2  International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  3. (a) No one shall be required to perform forced or compulsory labour; (b) Paragraph 3(a) shall not be held to preclude, in countries where imprisonment with hard labour may be imposed as a punishment for a crime, the performance of hard labour in pursuance of a sentence to such punishment by a competent court; (c) For the purpose of this paragraph the term “forced or compulsory labour” shall not include:  (i) Any work or service, not referred to in sub-paragraph (b), normally required of a person who is under detention in consequence of a lawful order of a court, or of a person during conditional release from such detention;  (ii) Any service of a military character and, in countries where conscientious objection is recognized, any national service required by law of conscientious objectors;  (iii) Any service exacted in cases of emergency or calamity threatening the life or well-being of the community;  (iv) Any work or service which forms part of normal civil obligations."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ed3e783102fcbba59bac257a12c2392b62ab9df0eadb6cfc9d11bebf87002095" ;
    cof:pageNumber "133"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "No one shall be held in slavery or servitude." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
