concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-39 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "39 1."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-39 ;
    values:originalText "The Committee shall elect its officers for a term of two years. They may be re-elected. 2. The Committee shall establish its own rules of procedure, but these rules shall provide, inter alia, that: (a) Twelve members shall constitute a quorum; (b) Decisions of the Committee shall be made by a majority vote of the members present." ;
    skos:definition "The Committee shall elect its officers for a term of two years. They may be re-elected. 2. The Committee shall establish its own rules of procedure, but these rules shall provide, inter alia, that: (a) Twelve members shall constitute a quorum; (b) Decisions of the Committee shall be made by a majority vote of the members present."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "499c4d947fbebdf125e618e41499d1492204dd7ee6c82a4051e4646b719e1fdb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "144"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Committee must elect officers and establish rules of procedure." ;
