concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-44 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44 International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-44 ;
    values:originalText "Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  The provisions for the implementation of the present Covenant shall apply without prejudice to the procedures prescribed in the field of human rights by or under the constituent instruments and the conventions of the United Nations and of the specialized agencies and shall not prevent the States Parties to the present Covenant from having recourse to other procedures for settling a dispute in accordance with general or special international agreements in force between them." ;
    skos:definition "Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  The provisions for the implementation of the present Covenant shall apply without prejudice to the procedures prescribed in the field of human rights by or under the constituent instruments and the conventions of the United Nations and of the specialized agencies and shall not prevent the States Parties to the present Covenant from having recourse to other procedures for settling a dispute in accordance with general or special international agreements in force between them."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cc82c09dc43895a720ed5fc76299c328eecd2a86043706f12f005fcaec205ef5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "148"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "States Parties can use other procedures for settling disputes." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
